# Independent review and merge roles

Feature PRs receive an independent Codex review. Claude Code is not a required
reviewer or merger. The operator delegates routine merges to a separate merge
agent and is not expected to read code or approve each ordinary merge.

When opening or updating a feature PR:

1. A reviewer that did not author the changes checks the full final diff,
   acceptance criteria and test evidence, and records the reviewed head/base.
2. Verify findings, fix real bugs on the same branch and review changed code
   again. Record reasons for declining findings. Keep trivial reviews proportionate.
3. Execution, risk, secrets, CI and runtime changes also receive a separate
   security review; research changes require appropriate quant/data review.
4. A merge agent that did not author the change checks current required CI,
   independent review, resolved blockers, a current base and a non-draft mergeable
   PR. It squash-merges with an expected head SHA and no administrator bypass.
5. GitHub unattended auto-merge stays disabled. LIVE/SHADOW/TESTNET, real capital,
   real credentials and live risk limits still require explicit operator approval.
   A merge never deploys. Shared GitHub credentials do not make subagents native
   approving reviewers or separate authorization boundaries.

Canonical workflow: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), Development workflow, and
[GitHub workflow](../../docs/GITHUB_WORKFLOW.md).
